# Active Directory Home Lab - Lab 01: Building a Domain Controller

## Overview

This lab demonstrates the deployment of a Windows Server Domain Controller in a VirtualBox environment. The goal was to build the foundation of an Active Directory infrastructure that will be expanded in future labs.

The server was promoted to a Domain Controller, DNS was configured, and the Active Directory Domain Services (AD DS) role was successfully installed.

---

## Objectives

- Install Windows Server
- Configure VirtualBox networking
- Configure a static IP address
- Install Active Directory Domain Services (AD DS)
- Promote the server to a Domain Controller
- Install and configure DNS
- Verify Active Directory installation

---

