## Challenges Encountered

During deployment, several configuration issues were resolved:

- Configured a static IP address for the Domain Controller.
- Added a Host-Only Adapter in VirtualBox to create an isolated Active Directory network.
- Resolved networking configuration between the NAT and Host-Only adapters.
- Successfully completed Domain Controller promotion after correcting the network configuration.

---

## Outcome

A fully functional Active Directory Domain Controller was successfully deployed and verified. This environment will serve as the foundation for future labs involving Organizational Units, users, groups, Group Policy, DNS, DHCP, and Windows client domain joining.
